what REDS %788, OPEN and booked in this lane: 189 tracked shell sources find the repository root by a directory nothing tracks (rishi/bin holds only the built binary), so a fresh clone, a detached worktree, and every checkout of tracked bytes refuse before reading a file. The row hands the SWEEP's timing to the fleet and leaves two repair doors unweighed -- sweep 189 files to a tracked sentinel, or track one file under rishi/bin and fix all 189 at once. A door chosen by argument is a door nobody measured. Extend root_finder_scan.sh with a --doors reading deriving each door's real file cost from the index rather than from a typed number: the finder population, the pen layouts that create the build sentinel and would keep making the old shape, whether the proposed tracked sentinel is exactly as discriminating (occurs at root and nowhere below), and whether anything under rishi/bin stands tracked today. Prove both doors on metal in a real detached worktree in the pen, where the build sentinel refuses and each repair resolves. No sweep this lap; no file outside this lane moves.
